{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3139","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3139","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3139\",\"parent_revision\":\"794d88ce7de64b01c89e9e4de3dacdeba556c832b71c2287683bd225e7069ae1\",\"root_revision\":\"794d88ce7de64b01c89e9e4de3dacdeba556c832b71c2287683bd225e7069ae1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEvery agent definition enumerates its MCP tools by exact name in `tools:` frontmatter. This couples MCP server code to agent frontmatter in both directions, and neither direction fails loudly.\\n\\nRemove or rename a tool on a server, and every agent still listing it carries a dead entry with no error raised. Add a tool to a server, and no agent can see it until every relevant `tools:` list is hand-edited \u2014 the tool is invisible rather than broken, so nothing surfaces the gap. As a maintainer, when I change an MCP server's tool set I have no signal telling me which agent definitions I have just desynchronised.\\n\\nMeasured behaviour, 2026-08-22, four probe agents with all definitions registered before spawning:\\n\\n| Declared `tools:` | Received |\\n|---|---|\\n| `Read, Grep, artifact_migrate, SendMessage` | 3 \u2014 Read, Grep, SendMessage |\\n| `Read, Grep, SendMessage` (control) | 3 \u2014 identical |\\n| `*` | 147 (full set) |\\n| `Read, mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__*, SendMessage` | full set, unrestricted |\\n\\nA nonexistent MCP name is dropped silently while the rest of the grant survives, so drift degrades quietly instead of erroring. `tools: *` grants everything. A server-scoped wildcard fails open \u2014 it grants the full set rather than restricting to that server \u2014 so the obvious workaround for hand-maintaining the lists is unusable, and dangerous in the permissive direction.\\n\\nTwo instances already present in the tree, both silent drops rather than broken agents:\\n\\n- `artifact_migrate` appears in the `tools:` list of 14 agent files. It does not exist on the backlog server \u2014 verified against `backlog_core/server.py` and two repo tests that assert its absence.\\n- Eleven MCP servers are referenced across agent definitions but are not connected in this checkout: `mcp__exa__`, `mcp__context7__`, `mcp__git-forensics__`, `mcp__github__`, a non-local `mcp__Ref__`, and others. `ecosystem-researcher` is written to depend on a firecrawl server it can never receive, and its body treats those tools as required rather than optional.\\n\\nImpact: an agent silently loses a capability its own definition claims it has, and behaves as though the tool were simply unavailable. The failure surfaces only as degraded agent output, at runtime, in whatever install it lands in.\\n\\nRelates to #2292 (consolidating the backlog server's flat tool list into action-based tools would shrink the surface this problem spans) and #3094 (audit of missing `Bash` access in agent `tools:` lists \u2014 the same class of frontmatter/capability mismatch).\\n\\n**User-provided context**: a CI check comparing every `tools:` entry across `plugins/**/agents/*.md` against the tools each server actually advertises, failing loudly on a name that resolves to nothing, in the same shape as the existing manifest-sync hook. It would subsume both cleanups above and turn the next occurrence into a build failure.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **agent tools: frontmatter drifts from mcp server tool lists with no enforcement and silent failure in both directions** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 measured 2026-08-22 while scoping the dispatch-contract work\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f81c5197471bd698b05a70af8a1760ca12c1023b0aa7138991494e491696a202\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQLLkNQ\"}"}